  "answer": "I'll start by reading the diagnosis skill and locating how special prices with dates are applied on the storefront API.The create path stores the special end date on the start-date field, and the price calculator then checks the start date twice, so a dated special never applies. I'll lock that in with a failing test, then fix both spots.Dated specials never reached the storefront because product creation stored the discount end date in the start-date field, and the catalogue price calculation then compared the start date against today a second time instead of the end date. The end date is now saved on the end-date field, and a special applies when the start date is already in the past and the end date is still in the future. An end date alone, or no dates at all, still discounts as before.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core -am test -Dtest=ProductPriceUtilsSpecialDateTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"admin REST create path and storefront API end to end\"], \"missing\": [\"integration fixture that posts a product with discount dates and reads the storefront price\"]}",
